	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Silverpine Forest runs south from the glades of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link} to the great wall of {link:gilneas}Gilneas{/link}. Dark pines crowd its hills, and to the east its shores fall away into the grey water of {red:lordamere-lake}Lordamere Lake{/red}. Once it was a quiet country of farms, orchards and mills. Now it is a land of the dead and the cursed. The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} hold its roads from the {link:the-sepulcher}Sepulcher{/link}, the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} hold an island fortress in the lake, and in the hills howl the wolf-men of a mad archmage of {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records the year when the first humans settled Silverpine, or which lord first claimed it. Its people farmed the valleys, tended orchards and worked the mills. Above the hamlet of {link:pyrewood-village}Pyrewood{/link} stood the keep of the noble {link:baron-silverlaine}Baron Silverlaine{/link}. When King {link:genn-greymane}Genn Greymane{/link} sealed his kingdom after the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, the {link:the-greymane-wall}Greymane Wall{/link} rose across the south of the forest, and the gates of {link:gilneas}Gilneas{/link} closed behind it. The folk of Silverpine were left on the northern side.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The Dark Lady has given her lieutenant {link:varimathras}Varimathras{/link} the task of taking the lands to the south, and Silverpine is the first step. {link:high-executor-hadrec}High Executor Hadrec{/link} commands the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} at the {link:the-sepulcher}Sepulcher{/link}, but his enemies are many. Rot Hide gnolls, raised and bound by the traitor mage {link:thule-ravenclaw}Thule Ravenclaw{/link}, carry corpses out of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link} to {link:fenris-isle}Fenris Isle{/link}. The worgen of {link:archmage-arugal}Archmage Arugal{/link} hunt the woods, and the villagers of {link:pyrewood-village}Pyrewood{/link} turn into beasts each night. At {link:ambermill}Ambermill{/link}, the wizards of {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} work on a secret of their own and guard the roads with a heavy hand. At the {link:the-greymane-wall}Greymane Wall{/link}, frightened human refugees gather before gates that will not open.

In these days, the paladins of {link:tyr-s-watch}Tyr's Watch{/link} have sent an agent to the Sepulcher, and a traveller of the {link:skyborne}Skyborne{/link} has come to the forest, bringing grief with her.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}.{/b} Deathguard, Deathstalkers, apothecaries and a dead archmage of {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link}, all serving {link:sylvanas-windrunner}the Dark Lady{/link} from the {link:the-sepulcher}Sepulcher{/link}.
• {b}The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}.{/b} The Rot Hide gnolls, the servants of {link:thule-ravenclaw}Thule Ravenclaw{/link} and the mindless dead of the old farms.
• {b}The worgen.{/b} The Moonrage and the Sons of {link:archmage-arugal}Arugal{/link}, feral wolf-men who answer, in part, to the archmage of {link:shadowfang-keep}Shadowfang Keep{/link}.
• {b}The {link:pyrewood-villagers}cursed of Pyrewood{/link}.{/b} Villagers who are human by day and beasts by night.
• {b}The wizards of {link:ambermill}Ambermill{/link}.{/b} Magi of the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link} and their guards, friendly to neither the living nor the dead of the north.
• {b}Beasts and murlocs.{/b} Worgs, grizzled bears, great spiders and the Vile Fin {link:murlocs}murlocs{/link} of the lakeshore.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Plague.{/b} In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link} the plague swept {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. The farmers of northern Silverpine died on their land and rose among the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}.
• {b}The Worgen.{/b} The wizards of {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link} fought the Scourge in the forest, and their own dead rose against them. Against the counsel of his peers, {link:archmage-arugal}Archmage Arugal{/link} called on powers from beyond the world, and the worgen came. They slaughtered the dead, then turned on the wizards. They took {link:baron-silverlaine}Baron Silverlaine{/link}'s keep, and Arugal made it his own.
• {b}The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}.{/b} In time the Forsaken came south out of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link} and made the {link:the-sepulcher}Sepulcher{/link} their stronghold in the forest.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Forest",
			text = [=[• The apothecaries say that ages ago a plague killed every living thing in the waters of Lordamere Lake.
• Three young mages once wove a single wand out of their apprentice wands, as a sign of friendship. One of them was {link:thule-ravenclaw}Thule Ravenclaw{/link}.
• A dead archmage at the {link:the-sepulcher}Sepulcher{/link} claims that {link:archmage-arugal}Arugal{/link} never had the power to make a worgen at all.]=],
		},
	},
})

